config CPU_ACCEL
	tristate "Single CPU accelerator prototype"
	depends on SMP
	depends on MMU
	depends on HOTPLUG_CPU
	depends on GENERIC_IRQ_MIGRATION
	help
	  Build the first experimental single-CPU accelerator control plane and
	  CPU-hotplug-backed lifecycle backend.

	  The prototype exposes /dev/cpu_accel. A control process selects one
	  online CPU, maps a shared control and sample area, and starts a bounded
	  timestamp workload. During the workload the CPU is removed from Linux
	  scheduling through CPU hotplug and runs at a dedicated hotplug handoff
	  state. This is a development experiment, not a production isolation
	  mechanism or a hard latency guarantee.
